# Local development secrets for `wrangler pages dev`.
#
#   cp .dev.vars.example .dev.vars
#
# `npm run dev` copies this file to `.dev.vars` for you if it is missing, so the
# copy above is only needed if you want to edit the values first.
#
# `.dev.vars` is gitignored and must NEVER be committed. Real values for
# Production and Preview live only in Cloudflare Pages encrypted environment
# variables — see docs/runbooks/website-setup.md.
#
# The defaults below are deliberately safe: they use Cloudflare's published
# Turnstile *test* keys and the ConsoleSink, so a fresh clone runs end to end
# with no Google account, no real secrets and no network writes.

# Which LeadSink the Function writes through: "console" | "google_sheet".
# Keep this as "console" for local dev unless you are specifically testing the
# Google Sheets path with your own throwaway sheet.
#
# This line matters more than it looks: `wrangler.toml` sets LEAD_SINK for what
# production gets, and `.dev.vars` overrides it locally (verified — `wrangler
# pages dev` shows LEAD_SINK as "(hidden)", i.e. from here, and leads print to
# the terminal). Delete this line and local submissions start failing with 502.
#
# NAMING: the CTO picked `google_sheet` (underscore) on 2026-10-13. wrangler.toml
# and the runbook both say that now; the hyphenated `google-sheet` still works
# but logs a deprecation warning, and is kept only for a value typed into the
# Cloudflare dashboard before this was settled. The `sheet` shorthand is gone.
LEAD_SINK="console"

# --- Turnstile ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Cloudflare's documented dummy secret key: always passes verification.
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/turnstile/troubleshooting/testing/
# Real value in Pages: Settings > Environment variables, encrypted.
#
# Swap in 2x0000000000000000000000000000000AA to exercise the 403 "bot" path
# locally: that test secret always *fails* verification.
# If this is unset entirely, the Function falls back to the always-pass test
# secret, so a fresh clone works with no configuration at all.
TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY="1x0000000000000000000000000000000AA"

# --- Google Sheets (only needed when LEAD_SINK="google_sheet") -----------------
# Leave these empty for normal local dev.
#
# The sheet id is the long id from the sheet URL:
#   https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/<THIS PART>/edit
#
# NAMING: the CTO has picked GOOGLE_SHEET_ID (2026-10-13). This is now the only
# name the Function reads — the older SHEET_ID from FOO-2 has been removed, so a
# leftover SHEET_ID is ignored and the sink fails with a named missing variable.
GOOGLE_SHEET_ID=""

# The service account's email, e.g. foodos-website@<project>.iam.gserviceaccount.com
# The sheet must be shared with this address as an Editor, or appends 403.
GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_EMAIL=""

# The service account's PEM private key, newlines escaped as \n and the whole
# value on ONE line. Taken from `private_key` in the downloaded JSON key.
# Never paste a real key into any file other than your local .dev.vars.
GOOGLE_PRIVATE_KEY=""

# Which tab/range to append to. Optional; defaults to "Leads".
# SHEET_RANGE="Leads"

# --- Optional tuning ----------------------------------------------------------
# All optional — the Function has working defaults for each.

# Extra CORS origins, comma separated. localhost/127.0.0.1 are always allowed,
# and in production the site and the Function share an origin, so this is only
# needed if the form is ever hosted somewhere else.
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS="https://foodos.ai,https://www.foodos.ai"

# Per-IP rate limit. Defaults to 5 requests per 10 minutes.
# RATE_LIMIT_MAX="5"
# RATE_LIMIT_WINDOW_SECONDS="600"
